  "reason": "The best result so far is config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, ResNet50, transformer, weighted) at 0.7131 accuracy. Evidence consistently shows scvi_n200 > scgpt > PCA, multiprofile > singleprofile, transformer ≥ avgpool, and weighted > concat. The primary remaining uncertainty is the image encoder: ResNet50 is a relatively modest backbone, while imagenet_vit_l (ViT-Large) is a substantially stronger visual encoder. Config_039 is a clean single-variable extension of config_033, swapping only ResNet50 → imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other components (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) fixed at their empirically best settings. As the final experiment in the budget, exploiting the strongest identified direction with the highest-impact untested variable (image encoder capacity) is the best use of the last slot, and a stronger visual representation could plausibly push accuracy above 0.7131."
}

